Significance: minor
Type: enhancement

Offline Mode: make the plugin usable in local development. Adds a dedicated dashboard landing page explaining why Offline Mode is active, listing every page that still works, with detection of local dev environments such as WordPress Studio and a notice when no internet connection is available. My Jetpack, Stats, Search, Social, VideoPress, Newsletter, Activity Log, and Subscribers are now shown in Offline Mode instead of hidden, matching a connected site's sidebar. Stats and Activity Log now boot the actual real dashboards (the same Odyssey Stats widget and Activity Log timeline a connected site sees) with their underlying WordPress.com API calls replaced by realistic sample data, instead of a bare connection wall or a hand-built substitute. Traffic charts, Top Posts, Referrers, the Locations map, and a sample activity timeline all render through the genuine product UI. Search, Social, and VideoPress render their real dashboards with sample data instead of a bare connection wall, clearly labeled as sample data with a link to the Offline Mode explanation; Social's Settings tab (auto-share toggle, Social Image Generator, link customization) and Newsletter's Settings tab are fully functional, with an honest explanation only where a feature (like Newsletter subscribers) fundamentally needs a live connection. Fixes the AI page showing a generic connection-error notice instead of an Offline Mode explanation. Removes duplicate Offline Mode messaging and the now-empty legacy dashboard tab bar. Fixes default connection-independent modules (like Jetpack Blocks) never activating on a site that has always been in Offline Mode.
